    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6762796d_25e2d0f0",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1831528
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-13T23:07:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since you already have `ok()` below `let _unused` is not necessary. Or if `let _unused` is preferred then the `ok()` below is not needed.\n\nI prefer `ok()` without `let _unused`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d05042b53b1d8c9c34387fb174e6853fd21285ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "11546d61_3d073cad",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-14T05:15:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So a while ago, I introduced a bug because I forgot to call .await. The previous pattern was:\n```\nlet _ \u003d txl.send(...).await;\n```\n\nThis doesn\u0027t protect you from failing to call await. The new pattern (requiring an Option\u003c()\u003e type) will protect you from failure to call `.await` and also not add the `unused result` warning.",
      "parentUuid": "6762796d_25e2d0f0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d05042b53b1d8c9c34387fb174e6853fd21285ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99333ba4_e2bdad74",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1831528
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T00:18:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we forget to call await, there should be:\n```\nwarning: unused implementer of `Future` that must be used\n   --\u003e system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs:270:21\n    |\n270 | /                     txl\n271 | |                         .send(Message::DelayedAdapterActions(DelayedActions::ConnectAllProfiles(\n272 | |                             device,\n273 | |                         )));\n    | |____________________________^\n    |\n    \u003d note: `#[warn(unused_must_use)]` on by default\n    \u003d note: futures do nothing unless you `.await` or poll them\n```\n\nAdding the `let _unused: Option\u003c()\u003e` doesn\u0027t really protect this bug since the writer can forget to add `let _unused...` too.\n\nTo actually protect us from bugs, maybe we should start using `--deny warnings` in our ebuild, since we have accumulated quite a few warnings already (and may want to add `-A improper_ctypes_definitions -A improper_ctypes -A unknown_lints` to allowlist warnings from generated code). Maybe we can have a use flags like USE\u003dfloss-nostrict to disable the `--deny warnings` for easier development but eventually production code will be free from warnings. How about that?",
      "parentUuid": "11546d61_3d073cad",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d05042b53b1d8c9c34387fb174e6853fd21285ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41c00ec5_4d91f353",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T01:32:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "https://github.com/rust-unofficial/patterns/blob/main/anti_patterns/deny-warnings.md\n\nBecause code and dependencies are split between AOSP and Chromium with third-party dependencies, this is going to be hard to do and enforce unilaterally.\n\nThe old pattern around awaits was to use `let _ \u003d txl.send(...).await` which was problematic. This can be used in conjunction with denying warnings locally but I don\u0027t think we can unilaterally enable it (even in CI).",
      "parentUuid": "99333ba4_e2bdad74",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 270,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "d05042b53b1d8c9c34387fb174e6853fd21285ca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1e02eb51_7ed7be27",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/suspend.rs",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 270,
      "author": {
        "id": 1831528
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T01:37:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that article, what\u0027s to be avoided is the `#[deny(warnings)[` embedded in code. But it says in Alternative section that `--deny warnings` as RUSTFLAGS is a better solution, which is what I was suggesting.\n\nStill I am okay with not `--deny warnings` by default until we are sure.",
      "parentUuid": "41c00ec5_4d91f353",
